{
  "_doc": "The weapon registry: recoil = the spray pattern, keyframes [shot index, up, right] in radians (linear between, the last held; empty = none) and recoveryTime = seconds for the spray index to fall to 10% once the trigger has rested one interval (exponential, CS2 recovery time; 0 or missing = at once; internal/game/recoil_shared.go, generated to the client). the client (web/assets/weapons/index.js) and the server (internal/game/weapons.go) both read this file. interval = seconds between shots; action = semi (one shot per click) | auto (hold) | bolt (one shot, then unscope and cycle for `cycle` s) | plant (The Big Diff, slot bomb: never fires; fire held in a site plants it, internal/game/rounds.go) | throw (grenades: the shot is the throw; mag = how many you may carry; grenade = {kind he|flash|smoke, fuse s, radius m, duration s}) | burst (one click fires `burst` rounds `burstGap` s apart, then `interval` s until the next burst); pellets = rays per shot (shotguns), each with its own seeded spread; class drives the kill reward (economy.json) and the buy menu; armorPen = fraction of damage through armor (CS armor ratio, default 0.5); penetration = fraction of the damage a bullet keeps after passing through a body (internal/game/penetration.go: a ray hits every player it crosses before a wall, nearest first, at most 3; each takes what is left x hit part x falloff x armor; teammates under mp_friendlyfire 0 take nothing but still slow it; 0 or missing = stops at the first body: shotgun pellets, melee; no penetration through the world); speed = max move speed as a fraction of the knife's (CS2 weapon speed / 250); falloff = damage multiplier per 12.7 m (CS range modifier, default 1); scope = {fov (vertical, radians), overlay lens|none}; spread in radians (base standing still, +move per m/s above 34% of the weapon's max speed (counter-strafe: stop and you're accurate), +air in the air, +belt x the empty fraction of the mag, x crouch when crouched); recoil.kick = pitch per shot, recoil.side = random yaw per shot; range in metres.",
